    "result_text": "All tests pass. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `salutation` field on the owner endpoint. The request may include an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR); the response returns `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nFollowing the existing patterns in the codebase (DTOs generated from `openapi.yml`, entity-derived fields as `@Transient` getters auto-mapped by MapStruct), the changes were:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` as an optional request field on `OwnerFields`, and `salutation` as a read-only derived field on `Owner`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `title` column/field (getter+setter), and a `@Transient getSalutation()` that composes the salutation, placed alongside the other derivations (`getLocality`, `getContactPreference`, etc.). MapStruct maps `title` and `salutation` by name automatically, so no mapper or function-pipeline changes were needed.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table so the value survives to `GET`.\n\nThe logic lives in one small getter with a single responsibility, and no existing class was expanded into a catch-all. The `AcceptanceTest` (the full suite) passes.",
